    "title": "Twelve nights on one star",
    "note": "Each row is one night of the allocation. The dim bar is astronomical night; the bright part is when the target is also above the airmass limit. The ticks are the twelve measurements your plan would take. Underneath is the spectral window of those twelve times - a property of the schedule alone, with no data in it.",
